      "description": "Requests slower than the histogram's top bucket. The service permits pickup 60s + worker 180s = 240s but content_request_duration_seconds stops at 60s, so p99 is extrapolated and UNDERSTATES the tail — count the overflow directly instead. During the 2026-07-27 outage p95 pinned at exactly 29.00s for 360 consecutive samples, the interpolation signature of 100% of requests sitting in the (10s, 30s] bucket. NOTE the bucket label is decimal-formatted: le=\"60.0\". Querying le=\"60\" returns nothing.",
